+Set `agent_selection_style = "outline"` under `[ui]` to replace the
+focused entry's background fill with accent-colored `[ … ]` brackets. The brackets
+mark the last nonblank content line, leaving group headings and spacer rows alone.
+This keeps selection markers one line high without adding rows or changing click
+targets. One right-edge column is reserved in this mode, so focus does not change
+title truncation. The default is `"fill"`. Spaces and collapsed views are unchanged.
+
 `row_gap` controls the blank terminal rows between entries, independently for the Agent and Space panels. It defaults to `0`, which packs entries together; set it to `1` to restore the previous spacing. It does not add spacing between the content lines declared in `rows`. Consecutive indented worktree children remain packed as one Space group.
 
